; Stand in as the game's version.dll. EU4 imports VERSION.dll; Windows loads the game-directory
; copy before the System32 one (version.dll is NOT a KnownDLL -- checked), so our DllMain runs
; before the game's main and the mod is present in EVERY launch, Steam's included.
;
; NO FORWARDERS ANY MORE (2026-08-28). These used to read `= pgt_version_orig.<name>`, which meant
; the user had to hand-copy System32's version.dll into the game directory under that private name
; -- the most error-prone step in installing the mod, and one whose failure kills the process at
; load with no window and no log. The target could never simply be "version": the loader resolves a
; forwarder's module by the normal search order, finds US, and a self-referential forwarder is a
; load-time failure.
;
; Each name below is now a real exported stub (proxy.h) that jumps through a pointer filled during
; DllMain from the system copy, loaded by absolute path. One file to install instead of two.
LIBRARY per-good-trade
EXPORTS
    GetFileVersionInfoA
    GetFileVersionInfoByHandle
    GetFileVersionInfoExA
    GetFileVersionInfoExW
    GetFileVersionInfoSizeA
    GetFileVersionInfoSizeExA
    GetFileVersionInfoSizeExW
    GetFileVersionInfoSizeW
    GetFileVersionInfoW
    VerFindFileA
    VerFindFileW
    VerInstallFileA
    VerInstallFileW
    VerLanguageNameA
    VerLanguageNameW
    VerQueryValueA
    VerQueryValueW
